KNOWNBUG: a requires atom that CALLS a constexpr static member function
template (requires(ok<U2>()) where ok's body references the enclosing
class's parameter) cannot be constant-folded by the satisfaction check;
the unviable constrained constructor survives and its body fails
conversion.  Exact shape of libstdc++ C++20 pair's
requires(_S_constructible<_U1, _U2>()) -- the remaining blocker for
cpp20_pair_converting_ctor / cpp20_map_basic.  The inline-atom variant
is CORE (cpp20_requires_class_param_atom).  Header-free.  FIX LEAD:
the call-atom fold must type-check the callee body with BOTH the
member's and the class's template maps in scope.  Flip to CORE when
fixed.
